// A payload-less enum is a bare C integer with no struct to walk, so `@generate` has nothing to
// synthesize into. This used to be silently ignored — the attribute read as if it had worked. It now
// names the working alternative: a plain enum takes a retroactive `implements` (see tests/enum_map_key).
@generate(Equatable)
enum Color { Red, Green, Blue }
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
